<!--MachineBlocks — MBML documentation

  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.mbml.DomainModel-->
<mbml:DomainModel xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:mbcore="com.machineblocks.bml.core"
  xmlns:mbml="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.mbml">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    A guide to the MachineBlocks domain Block hierarchy
  </is>
  <documentation>
    MachineBlocks domain types under com.machineblocks.bml.core:
    
    Block — abstract domain base (baseType Entity). Carries name, presets aggregation, and
    basePresets association.
    ConfigProfile — abstract parameter surface (baseType Block). Defines the native properties whose
    conventional home is the config profile: calibration, printer profile, and clearances that
    follow the printer. Not a resolver constraint — settings may still override any parameter.
    Content blocks do not extend ConfigProfile.
    ConfigSet — abstract collection of ConfigProfile values (baseType Block). A concrete set
    extends ConfigSet and fills profiles. The SCAD target emits that set as
    mb__…__func__config. A Block File uses that file, offers configProfile in the
    customizer, and assigns mb_config once in Hidden from that function. The main
    call passes mb_config. Compile can name the set.
    Otherwise the first ConfigSet in the project blocks folder is used, otherwise a
    ConfigSet from the machineblocks core. The function is an if/else over one
    function per profile (see config:DefaultConfigSet).
    CompositeBlock — Block with default _parts aggregation for child block instances.
    NativeBlock — final leaf geometry Block. Maps 1:1 to the native geometry primitive at render
      time. baseType is ConfigProfile. Together with ConfigProfile, the SSOT for all native MachineBlocks
      parameters: config-conventional properties are defined on ConfigProfile, brick and feature
      properties on NativeBlock. Uses children for nested native geometry
      instead of _parts. Must not be used as baseType for custom Block definitions.
    Set — CompositeBlock for LEGO-style builds: palette via presets, placed instances in _parts,
      assembly order in _steps.
    Step — final assembly instruction Block. baseType is org.blockml.bml.core.Block (framework
      Block), not mbcore:Block / Entity — a sibling outside the Entity → mbcore:Block tree.
      part association references a placed _parts instance by bml:id; document order in _steps is
      build order.
    
    Hierarchy: Entity → mbcore:Block → ConfigProfile → NativeBlock. ConfigSet stays under
    mbcore:Block. CompositeBlock → Set stays under mbcore:Block. NativeBlock is final.
    Step sits on org.blockml.bml.core.Block → Step.
    
    Class identity is the Block FQN. Instance identity inside composition uses bml:id (nested paths
    use ::). There is no separate Placement type — direction, offset, and related placement data
    live on the placed instances.
  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="mbml:TypeSystem" relation="ReadNext">
      Next — MachineBlocks type package overview.
    </see>
    <see type="mbcore:Block" relation="Defines">
      Abstract MachineBlocks domain Block.
    </see>
    <see type="mbcore:ConfigProfile" relation="Defines">
      Config-conventional native parameters. NativeBlock extends ConfigProfile.
    </see>
    <see type="mbcore:ConfigSet" relation="Defines">
      Selectable ConfigProfile collection and the SCAD config function.
    </see>
    <see type="mbcore:NativeBlock" relation="Defines">
      Final leaf geometry Block — native parameter SSOT together with ConfigProfile.
    </see>
    <see type="mbcore:CompositeBlock" relation="Defines">
      Composable Block with _parts.
    </see>
    <see type="mbcore:Set" relation="Defines">
      LEGO-style set with _steps.
    </see>
    <see type="mbcore:Step" relation="Defines">
      Assembly step — framework Block (org.blockml.bml.core.Block), not mbcore:Block.
    </see>
    <see type="core:Block" relation="SeeAlso">
      Framework Block — baseType of Step.
    </see>
  </references>
</mbml:DomainModel>
